{
  "v": 1,
  "kind": "take_cases",
  "about": "N1's take rule (the NBA model's fair, plan 5(f) generalised) and N2's (pregame 90-95c favourites, the sports hunt's forward test), hand-worked: deskd's take_decide (include/deskd/strat/take.h, which says the rule in full) and tools/nba_gate.py (n1 and n2) must both give every 'want' here, so the replay measures the rule the lane trades. Synthetic games and tickers; no account data.",
  "how": "A case's input is base[mode] with the case's 'in' laid over it, and its params are params[mode] with the case's 'params' laid over them: an object is merged key by key (recursively), any other value replaces (null clears it). 'want' is either {'take': {ticker, side, price, count, fee, edge, dir}} or {'pull': CODE, 'edge': the pulled route's edge or null, 'dir': 'A', 'B' or null (the game's own checks)}.",
  "units": "Prices and money are the contract's decimal strings in dollars (exactly 4 decimals); sizes are contracts (0.01 steps); times are ms on one clock; game_used and game_cap are dollars; fee_mult is the market's fee_multiplier. A team's price is the ask it buys at, or 1 - the other market's bid it sells at. fee = 0.07 x mult x count x price x (1 - price), rounded up to $0.000001 and then up to the cent (gw/fees.h kalshi_fee_order_cent). MODEL: edge = the fair for the team - its price - fee / count, rounded down to $0.0001 for 'want'. FAV_PREGAME has no edge (0): its band is the rule. A leg's position is the lane's own, signed (YES > 0); sys_position is Systematic's in the market, every lane's, signed, and sys_buying and sys_selling what is left of its working orders there on each side; inventory is the lane's limit a market, in contracts (gw's SYS_CEILING inventory). A route's count is also at most max(inventory, |x|) - x - w, in whole steps, where x is the market sent to's sys_position for a BUY (-sys_position for a SELL) and w its sys_buying (sys_selling): none, and the route stops at INVENTORY, after GAME_CAP and before CLIP. prev_poll_ms is the score's last poll before first_seen_ms (0: none), so the state changed between the two. With stale_only a route stops at TOUCH_AFTER_SCORE, before the touch's own age is checked, when prev_poll_ms is 0 or first_seen_ms - prev_poll_ms is over max_poll_gap_ms (ms).",
